#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:3
msgid "Edit Prediction"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:5
msgid ""
"Edit Prediction is how Zed's AI code completions work: an LLM predicts the "
"code you want to write. Each keystroke sends a new request to the edit "
"prediction provider, which returns individual or multi-line suggestions you "
"accept by pressing `tab`."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:8
msgid ""
"The default provider is [Zeta, an open source model developed by Zed]"
"(https://zed.dev/blog/zeta2), but you can also use [other providers](#other-"
"providers) like GitHub Copilot, Mercury Coder, and Codestral."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:10
msgid "Configuring Zeta"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:12
msgid ""
"To use Zeta, [sign in](../authentication.md#what-features-require-signing-"
"in). Once signed in, predictions appear as you type."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:15
msgid ""
"You can confirm that Zeta is properly configured by opening the [Settings "
"Editor](zed://settings/edit_predictions.providers) (`Cmd+,` on macOS or "
"`Ctrl+,` on Linux/Windows) and searching for `edit_predictions`. The "
"`provider` field should be set to `Zed AI`."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:17
msgid "Or verify this in your settings.json:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:21 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:43
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:181 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:193
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:209 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:223
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:258 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:280
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:296
msgid "\"edit_predictions\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:22 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:194
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:210 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:259
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:281 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:297
msgid "\"provider\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:22
msgid "\"zed\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:27
msgid "The Z icon in the status bar also indicates Zeta is active."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:29
msgid "Pricing and Plans"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:31
msgid ""
"The free plan includes 2,000 Zeta predictions per month. The [Pro plan](../"
"ai/plans-and-usage.md) removes this limit. See [Zed's pricing page](https://"
"zed.dev/pricing) for details."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:33
msgid "Switching Modes"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:35
msgid "Edit Prediction has two display modes:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:37
msgid ""
"`eager` (default): predictions are displayed inline as long as it doesn't "
"conflict with language server completions"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:38
msgid ""
"`subtle`: predictions only appear inline when holding a modifier key (`alt` "
"by default)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:40
msgid "Toggle between them via the `mode` key:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:44
msgid "\"mode\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:44
msgid "\"eager\" // or \"subtle\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:48
msgid "Or directly via the UI through the status bar menu:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:50
msgid ""
"![Edit Prediction status bar menu, with the modes toggle.](https://zed.dev/"
"img/edit-prediction/status-bar-menu.webp)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:52
msgid "Note that edit prediction modes work with any prediction provider."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:54
msgid "Default Key Bindings"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:56
msgid ""
"On macOS and Windows, you can accept edit predictions with `alt-tab`. On "
"Linux, `alt-tab` is often used by the window manager for switching windows, "
"so `alt-l` is the default key binding for edit predictions."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:58
msgid ""
"In `eager` mode, you can also use the `tab` key to accept edit predictions, "
"unless the completion menu is open, in which case `tab` accepts LSP "
"completions. To use `tab` to insert whitespace, you need to dismiss the "
"prediction with <kbd class=\"keybinding\">escape\\|escape</kbd> before "
"hitting `tab`."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:60
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">editor: accept next word edit prediction</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-cmd-right\\|alt-k</kbd>) can be used to accept the "
"current edit prediction up to the next word boundary. <code "
"class=\"hljs\">editor: accept next line edit prediction</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-cmd-down\\|alt-j</kbd>) can be used to accept the "
"current edit prediction up to the new line boundary."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:63
msgid "Configuring Edit Prediction Keybindings"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:65
msgid "Keybinding Example: Always Use Tab"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:67
msgid ""
"To always use `tab` for accepting edit predictions, regardless of whether "
"the LSP completions menu is open, you can add the following to your keymap:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:69
msgid ""
"Open the keymap editor with <code class=\"hljs\">zed: open keymap</code> "
"(<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-k cmd-s\\|ctrl-k ctrl-s</kbd>), search for "
"`AcceptEditPrediction`, right click on the binding for `tab` and hit `edit`. "
"Then change the context the binding is active in to just `Editor && "
"edit_prediction` and save it."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:71 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:92
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:113
msgid "Alternatively, you can put the following in your `keymap.json`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:76 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:97
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:118
msgid "\"context\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:76 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:97
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:118
msgid "\"Editor && edit_prediction\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:77 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:125
msgid "\"bindings\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:78 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:99
msgid "\"tab\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:78 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:99
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:120 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:123
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:126
msgid "\"editor::AcceptEditPrediction\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:84
msgid ""
"After that, <kbd class=\"keybinding\">tab\\|tab</kbd> remains available for "
"accepting LSP completions."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:86
msgid "Keybinding Example: Always Use Alt-Tab"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:88
msgid ""
"To stop using `tab` for accepting edit predictions and always use `alt-tab` "
"instead, unbind the default `tab` binding in the eager edit prediction "
"context:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:90
msgid ""
"Open the keymap editor with <code class=\"hljs\">zed: open keymap</code> "
"(<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-k cmd-s\\|ctrl-k ctrl-s</kbd>), search for "
"`AcceptEditPrediction`, right click on the binding for `tab` and delete it."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:98 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:119
msgid "\"unbind\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:105
msgid ""
"After that, `alt-tab` remains available for accepting edit predictions, and "
"on Linux `alt-l` does too unless you unbind it."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:107
msgid "Keybinding Example: Rebind Both Tab and Alt-Tab"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:109
msgid ""
"To move both default accept bindings to something else, unbind them and add "
"your replacement:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:111
msgid ""
"Open the keymap editor with <code class=\"hljs\">zed: open keymap</code> "
"(<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-k cmd-s\\|ctrl-k ctrl-s</kbd>), search for "
"`AcceptEditPrediction`, right click on the binding for `tab` and delete it. "
"Then right click on the binding for `alt-tab`, select \"Edit\", and record "
"your desired keystrokes before hitting saving."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:120
msgid "\"alt-tab\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:121
msgid ""
"// Add this as well on Windows/Linux\n"
"      // \"alt-l\": \"editor::AcceptEditPrediction\",\n"
"      \"tab\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:126
msgid "\"ctrl-enter\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:132
msgid ""
"In this case, because the binding contains the modifier `ctrl`, it will be "
"used to preview the prediction in subtle mode, or when the completions menu "
"is open."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:134
msgid "Cleaning Up Older Keymap Entries"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:136
msgid ""
"If you configured edit prediction keybindings before Zed `v0.229.0`, your "
"`keymap.json` may have entries that are now redundant."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:138
msgid ""
"**Old tab workaround**: Before `unbind` existed, the only way to prevent "
"`tab` from accepting edit predictions was to copy all the default non-edit-"
"prediction `tab` bindings into your keymap alongside a custom "
"`AcceptEditPrediction` binding. If your keymap still contains those copy-"
"pasted entries, delete them and use a single `\"unbind\"` entry as shown in "
"the examples above."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:140
msgid ""
"**Renamed context**: The `edit_prediction_conflict` context has been "
"replaced by `edit_prediction && (showing_completions || "
"in_leading_whitespace)`. Zed automatically migrates any bindings that used "
"`edit_prediction_conflict`, so no changes are required on your end."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:142
msgid "Disabling Automatic Edit Prediction"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:144
msgid ""
"You can disable edit predictions at several levels, or turn them off "
